From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:07:44 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 258/297] Meridian: Send a report
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Send a report…" in Settings › General › Help, in ⌘T, and as a link by the
errors of the Ask panel, Chat and the command bar's Ask. A sheet shows
everything the report contains before anything leaves, editable: "What
happened?", the Meridian and system versions and CPU, Settings › AI (who
answers, agent access, consent, other agents), the AIs and coding agents
found (names, models for local/cloud ones, each found CLI's --version), the
agents that used Meridian this session, the updater's state, and the last
200 lines of Meridian's own errors (Ask and provider failures with the CLI's
exit code and stderr tail or the HTTP status and body, failed agent tools,
update failures, and LOG(WARNING)+ from chrome/browser/meridian), kept in
memory for this run only.

Everything is scrubbed in report.cc (unit-tested): addresses become [link]
(a server on this computer keeps scheme://host:port), keys and tokens
(sk-, ghp_, github_pat_, AIza, xox, AKIA, JWTs, Bearer, key=…, long
base64/hex) [hidden], e-mails [email], the account and full name [name],
and any home folder ~. The person's words and edits are scrubbed again on
the way out, and the boxes show what left.

Nothing is sent by itself: Copy report (Markdown to the clipboard), Save
as file… (a .md; --meridian-test-save-report for tests), and Open an
issue on GitHub (a prefilled, short issue under 2000 characters, with the
full report on the clipboard to paste).

